slide('record','Save an operation’s inputs, output, and timing.',code('''result, record = event(
    "inspect_notebook", {},
    lambda: {"python": platform.python_version()},
)
''')+'\n<ReceiptFlow />','The event helper runs the supplied function and returns two objects. result is what the caller needs; record describes the operation with its arguments, output, timing, and any error. We save that record before exporting a trace. If export fails, we can send the saved record again without repeating a refund or another model request.')
slide('tool-scope','Export the saved operation as an Agent Lens span.',code('''with tracing.Tool(
    name=record["name"],
    arguments=record["arguments"],
    result=record["result"],
    tool_call_id=record["id"],
    started_at=stamp(record["started_at"]),
    ended_at=stamp(record["ended_at"]),
) as span:
    if record.get("error"):
        span.record_error(RuntimeError(record["error"]))
''',focus='1-3|4-7|8-10|all')+'\n<div class="bottom-note">`my_tool_span` turns this saved record into a tool span. Export can be retried without repeating the operation.</div>','Map each field to the record from the previous slide. Tool creates a span with the operation name, inputs, output, and timestamps; record_error attaches the recorded failure. This function exports an event that already happened. The full notebook function returns its span identity so the execution can link back to Agent Lens.')
