slide('dispatch','Dispatch lookup_invoice to your function.',code('''def my_dispatch(name, arguments, world, invoice_tool, call_tool):
    if name == "lookup_invoice":
        return world, invoice_tool(world, **arguments)
    return call_tool(world, name, arguments)
''',focus='1-3|4|all')+'\n<div class="bottom-note">Both paths return `(world, result)`. The invoice path preserves `world`; write tools may change it.</div>','Trace two inputs through this function. lookup_invoice calls the participant function and returns the same world with its lookup result. get_account takes the existing call_tool path. Both return a pair of account state and observation, so the caller can append the observation consistently. A write tool may return changed state.')
exercise('handoff','Append the action and its result to the next request.','3 · Pass observations to the agent','Complete my_dispatch and my_observation. Append the action and actual result to a new message list, keeping the previous request unchanged.','Test my tool-to-model handoff','Open the four handoff tabs. Match the action, Python arguments, returned payments, and two appended messages.','loop')
slide('messages','Include the tool observation in the conversation history.',code('''return messages + [
    {"role": "assistant", "content": json.dumps(action)},
    {"role": "user", "content": "Tool observation: " + json.dumps(result)},
]
''',focus='1-2|3|all')+'\n<p>The next model request includes both the action it selected and the returned payments. It can use those records to decide which payment to refund.</p>\n<div class="bottom-note">The user-role message carries tool data in this JSON protocol. It is not a new customer instruction.</div>','The model cannot see a Python return value unless the executor includes it in a later request. Append the chosen action and its result to a new list so the previous request stays available for inspection. This executor uses JSON actions and a user message containing the observation; it is not using the OpenAI tool-message protocol.')
