slide('retry-identity','A stable operation_id prevents a repeated write.','<RetryIdentity />','In notebook step 3, use the free local timeout practice. Predict the member count, trigger the timeout, and compare reading status with same-ID and new-ID retries. Reset between alternatives. This uses Python only, changes no saved employee run, and makes no model request. Illustration of simulator.execute after a committed provisioning request. The same operation_id and identical arguments return the stored receipt with replayed=true. A new operation_id is a new mutation and can add a duplicate membership. Reusing an ID with different arguments is rejected. The recorded onboarding recovery read status instead of retrying, so this diagram explains tool behavior rather than claiming this branch occurred in that run.')
