slide('editor','Management would like to automate management.','<p class="big">Give the editor the current instructions, verification skill, and execution record. It will propose two alternative harnesses for us to review and test.</p>\n<div class="two-col"><div><h2>It may edit</h2><p>Instructions, skills, and bounded workflow rules.</p></div><div><h2>Keep fixed</h2><p>The model, tested tools, fixtures, grader, and budget controls.</p></div></div>\n<div class="bottom-note">The notebook controller runs the tests and records which harness the editor chose.</div>','The editor uses the same fixed model, but its request is to revise the harness rather than resolve a customer ticket. We supply the current configuration and a saved execution. The permitted edits are instructions, the verification skill, and bounded workflow rules. Tools and scoring stay fixed so any measured difference concerns the harness we changed.')
for n,title,caption,narration in [
    (1,'Propose two edits to the same starting harness.',
     'Both candidates receive the parent harness and the same starting execution. Read each diff before testing it.',
     'Propose asks the editor for two competing changes, such as clearer verification instructions or a mandatory completion check. A and B start from the same parent. Neither receives the other candidate’s test result at this point. We review their saved configurations before allowing the probes.'),
    (2,'Run each candidate from the original account state.',
     'Probe executes A and B separately. Each starts with the same ticket and an unchanged copy of its account.',
     'If candidate A has already issued a refund, B must not inherit that refunded account. The controller resets the case before each probe. Compare the actions and returned state of both runs; a successful tool response alone does not tell us the ticket was handled correctly.'),
    (3,'Compare the probe results before selecting a harness.',
     'The dashed paths carry test records to Compose, which can select, combine, or retain the parent.',
     'Compose receives the proposed configurations and both execution records. It can choose A or B, combine parts of them, or retain the parent. Its rationale explains that choice, but the choice still needs an execution. The solid paths show versions; colors identify alternatives rather than scores.'),
    (4,'Execute the harness returned by the composition decision.',
     'The controller constructs the selected harness and runs it before saving it for the next task.',
     'A combination may differ from both tested candidates, so we run the returned configuration as its own probe. A Retain decision also runs through this step without inventing a new executable version. We can then inspect the specific execution associated with the decision.'),
    (5,'Save the selected harness and a lesson for onboarding.',
     'The next round receives the selected version, its execution record, and the lesson’s stated limits.',
     'Reflect asks the editor what it learned from the selected run and where that conclusion may not apply. We keep the lesson with that run, then execute the selected harness on onboarding before proposing more changes. This carried-harness teaching protocol differs from the full upstream Harness² cross-task procedure.'),
]:
    slide('branch-'+str(n),title,(f'<ImprovementBranches :level="{n}" />' if n < 5 else '<RoundTransfer />')+f'\n<div class="bottom-note">{caption}</div>',narration)
slide('propose-code','Give the editor the starting execution and harness.',code('''experience = [run_employee(session, case, parent, prefix + "starting", **hooks)]
editor_decision(
    session, round_number, "propose", parent, experience,
    tool_writer=my_tool_span, model_writer=my_model_span,
)
''',focus='1|2-4|all')+'\n<div class="bottom-note">`experience` contains the starting run’s actions and results. Final-case grades are excluded from the editor’s request.</div>','Conceptual variable names match the visible controller; actual notebook uses _s,_case,_parent,_prefix,_f. It passes prior_experience from round1 into round2. Ask which input would be inappropriate: final-test scores.')
exercise('propose','Review the proposed instruction and workflow changes.','6 · Improve twice','Read the visible controller. Ask for two changes, then inspect Candidate A’s diff and rationale. Mark the review checkbox only after reading the files.','Round 1 · Ask for two competing changes','The next action is Review and test candidate A. Explain what behavior A is intended to change.')
slide('probe-code','Construct and execute the proposed harness.',code('''harness = Harness(**decision["harness"])
run = run_employee(session, case, harness, prefix + phase, **hooks)
assert run["harness_fingerprint"] == decision["fingerprint"]
''',focus='1|2-3|all')+'\n<p>Each probe receives a fresh copy of the account state. The fingerprint check verifies that it used the harness returned in the saved decision.</p>\n<div class="bottom-note">This tests the proposed configuration; reading its rationale alone cannot establish its effect.</div>','The editor returns a structured harness in its decision. The controller constructs that harness, executes it on a reset case, and checks the recorded content fingerprint against the decision. That comparison catches running the wrong version. It says nothing about whether the selected instructions are good; the account scorer answers that separately.')
exercise('probes','Run both candidates and inspect their tool sequences.','6 · Improve twice','Review and test A, then review and test B. Follow each result into Agent Lens and look for the behavior its proposal promised.','Round 1 · Review and test candidate A; then candidate B','Both started from the same billing state. You can identify which changed files were used in each run.')
slide('completion-guard','Require a passing check of the current state before finish.','<CompletionGuard />','The loop stores last_check with passed and the digest of world. With verify_before_finish true, finish is rejected if that check is absent, failed, or no longer matches the current state. This is a runtime completion rule. check_work gives public development feedback; the independent final scorer separately checks entire expected accounts and the required resolution.')
shot('gate-screen','This candidate required a check before completion.','visual-v030-pending-verification.png',LENS+'9633d416f5fce6aaa0124ab6ddc38c46','Find the rejected finish, check_work, and accepted finish.','Recorded candidate B changed verify_before_finish from false to true. It produced the explicit check sequence. Spans: rejected finish 9ed1e7824138ec0e, check_work 2d49d1d8d3ddeb5d, accepted finish 3e19e007d013d4d2. This is a behavior change, not yet evidence of better quality.')
slide('gate-detail','The completion gate required a check_work call.','<div class="annotated"><CaptureDetail src="/images/visual-v030-pending-verification.png" :x="580" :y="251" :width="690" :height="185" label="Native finish error: Check the current work before submitting" /><div class="annotations"><p><code>verify_before_finish</code> blocked the first finish.</p><p>The following <code>check_work</code> call satisfied the gate.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">The account result still passed. The editor had to decide whether the additional gate was worth keeping.</div>','Crop x580,y251,w690,h185 from the unchanged1280x720 native capture. Gate behavior is confirmed by the subsequent check_work and accepted finish spans, not inferred from the proposal title.')
slide('probe-comparison','Compare the added checks with the resulting account state.','<ProbeComparison />','Recorded first-round probe A used the parent harness: get_account, refund_payment, get_account, finish. Probe B used verify_before_finish=true: the same first three calls, a rejected finish, check_work, and an accepted finish. Both independent account checks passed. Tool-call counts are four and six for these development probes, distinct from the later final-evaluation totals. Source: the v0.3.0 rehearsal journal pending/round-1/probe-a and probe-b, linked through the native conversations on the preceding slides.')
slide('keep','The editor retained the parent after comparing the probes.','<RetainExecution />\n<div class="bottom-note"><a href="https://forge.coreweave.com/agent-lens/wandb/forge-workshop-kit/conversations/c04f575608c6f43d99e1b7b428a23791">Read the recorded composition rationale ↗</a></div>','Ask learners for their optional A/B/retain reasoning before showing this composition. Their notebook notes are not provided to the editor. Open this saved composition if time allows. The editor’s rationale was that the mandatory gate added work while the parent already produced a correct billing outcome. It retained the parent. The controller still runs the selected configuration because every composition receives a confirming execution, including KEEP. The executable content remains unchanged.')
exercise('compose','Test the selected harness before carrying it forward.','6 · Improve twice','Before requesting composition, optionally choose A, B, the parent, or a combination and cite a probe result in the notebook. Then ask the editor, compare its reasoning with yours, and test the selected files.','Compare probes and request a composition → Review and test the composition → Save the tested version and its lesson','The chosen execution matches the decision. If it retained the parent, explain why the files are unchanged.')
slide('reflection','Save the lesson with the run that supports it.',code('''review = reflect_execution(
    session, round_number, run,
    tool_writer=my_tool_span, model_writer=my_model_span,
)
adopted = {
    "harness": chosen_harness,
    "lesson": review["lesson"],
    "limits": review["limits"],
    "execution": run["stage_id"],
}
''',focus='1-4|5-8|all')+'\n<p>The next round receives this selected harness and the saved lesson. Keeping the execution reference lets us inspect the observation behind the editor’s conclusion.</p>','Explanatory excerpt, not a drop-in full function. The actual controller falls back to the parent if the chosen execution does not complete. The lesson is agent-authored interpretation backed by a saved run.')
exercise('round-two','Use the selected harness to start the onboarding round.','6 · Improve twice','Round 2 starts with the version and lesson kept after billing. Propose, review, test, compose, test again, and save the result.','Round 2 · Ask for two competing changes; follow the current action','Explain what the previous lesson influenced and what the new execution showed. Do not assume a billing lesson transfers.')
slide('round-two-result','The second round changed the verification skill.','<div class="two-col"><div><h2>Recorded edit</h2><p>Check that the intended account change exists exactly once and that unrelated state stayed unchanged.</p></div><div><h2>Recorded choice</h2><p>Keep the completion gate off. Use the revised skill with the existing workflow.</p></div></div>\n<div class="bottom-note"><a href="'+LENS+'a39aede201a0fe7320092976c0501e42">Decision ↗</a> · <a href="'+LENS+'d641da20ff5e553866a93a3c12bee913">Execution of the chosen files ↗</a></div>','In the recorded onboarding round, the editor selected a more specific verification skill while leaving verify_before_finish off. Open the decision to read its rationale, then the chosen execution to inspect how the agent used those files. The next slide shows the exact changed sentence.')
slide('skill-diff','The skill makes the final check more specific.','<div class="diff"><div class="del">− Verify the account before claiming completion.</div><div class="add">+ Verify the account before claiming completion: confirm the intended change is present exactly once (no duplicate side effects) and that unrelated payments, memberships, and subscriptions are unchanged.</div></div><div class="bottom-note">Actual changed sentence in the recorded verification skill. The timeout and operation_id instructions above it stayed unchanged.</div>','Source .workshop/v030-pending/journal.json, pending/round-1/compose and pending/round-2/compose verification_skill. Display is an exact excerpt of the changed sentence. Round2 selected that skill with verify_before_finish=false. Link to preceding decision and execution; no attribution of final-quality gain.')
slide('rsi','The next round tests changes to the previous selection.','<RoundTransfer :recorded="true" />','Recursive self-improvement here means that an agent evaluates executions of a harness, proposes revisions, and later examines work done under the selected revision. The retained lesson supplies context for the next attempt. The language model’s weights never change. Our workshop carries a selected harness between two tasks; the upstream Harness² procedure has a broader recursion and experience-library design.')
slide('freeze','Freeze three harnesses for the fresh-case comparison.','<EvaluationMatrix />','Final cases: already-refunded, two-invoices, onboarding-recovery, clarify-access. Their files are public for teaching but are excluded from improvement context. The starting version is the configured tested employee, not the deliberately blank opening illustration.')
exercise('final','Compare all three versions on fresh tickets.','7 · Compare fresh tickets','Freeze the versions and run the final comparison. Use the saved-ticket selector to align the starting, manual, and agent-selected outputs.','Freeze versions and run 12 evaluations','Follow a score to its account state, judge reason, trace, and harness. Keep unavailable judgments separate from wrong answers.')
